d SaLuSa  secundus the Fremen eventually spread to  other planets including harmon tap  before eventually stopping on dune  though poor Turin is considered by some  to be the original Planet of the Fremen  it is said in terminology of the  Imperium but there are clues in their  language and mythology that show far  more ancient planetary roots the Firman  people are organized into groups  communities called CJIs each seat is  built within one of the numerous rocky  formations that exist sporadically  throughout the sands of Arrakis leading  each seat is an eon a leader who ascends  to his position by challenging his  predecessor in combat thus proving  himself the strongest member of the  tribe the fuhrmann justice system also  primarily relies on trial by combat  the Fremen are some of the best  hand-to-hand warriors in the entire  universe the harsh conditions of the  planet doom have forced them to be so in  the first book in the series Paul  Atreides teaches the Fremen warriors the  weirding way and with this they are able  to overthrow the imperial sardick our  soldiers who were previously unbeatable  as I mentioned earlier water also played  a vital role in Furman culture to the  Fremen people of Arrakis water was truly  life there was almost no water on the  surface of Arrakis for this reason  Freeman's survival demanded that they  conserve against the unnecessary loss of  water at all cost  all freeman we're still suits which are  full-body filtration systems which  reclaim the body's water the wearer of a  still suit would lose only a thimbleful  of water per day and be able to survive  for four weeks in the open desert  without the still suit a person would  die in the desert Sun within hours in  Furman culture the water of each  person's body belongs to the tribe when  a freeman dies the tribe conserves their  water by distilling it from the dead  body the Fremen use wind traps to  collect water from their atmosphere this  water is preserved in undergroun